    "comment": {
      "comments": [
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12429774/comment/13045018",
          "id": "13045018",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=sarowe",
            "name": "sarowe",
            "key": "steve_rowe",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258"
            },
            "displayName": "Steven Rowe",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "David, I tried to apply your patch, but it failed (using \"patch\") - maybe partly because the patch is in git format?  I don't use git, so it's tough for me to review issues with git formatted patches.\n\nI went and looked at the DateTools.java and compared it to your patch, and things have changed significantly since you wrote the patch, especially as a result of Uwe's changes from LUCENE-1472.  Could you take a look at that issue, see if it resolves (enough of) the problems you addressed in your patch to make this issue now obsolete?  If not, could you regenerate the patch (diff/patch format please)?",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=sarowe",
            "name": "sarowe",
            "key": "steve_rowe",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=steve_rowe&avatarId=37258"
            },
            "displayName": "Steven Rowe",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "created": "2011-06-06T18:38:13.181+0000",
          "updated": "2011-06-06T18:38:13.181+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12429774/comment/13045113",
          "id": "13045113",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=dsmiley",
            "name": "dsmiley",
            "key": "dsmiley",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?ownerId=dsmiley&avatarId=10110",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&ownerId=dsmiley&avatarId=10110",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&ownerId=dsmiley&avatarId=10110",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&ownerId=dsmiley&avatarId=10110"
            },
            "displayName": "David Smiley",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "America/New_York"
          },
          "body": "This is an updated patch.\n* The former \"DateFormats\" class was used as a value in a ThreadLocal which isn't a good idea as it hampers class reloading.\n* Improvements to a switch statement to benefit from fall-through.\n* Removed a pointless conversion to Calendar in timeToString()\n* Moved functionality to Resolution enum, and used arrays of Resolutions indexed by format length instead of large if-else or switch blocks for format & parse. The ramification is 48 fewer lines of code.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=dsmiley",
            "name": "dsmiley",
            "key": "dsmiley",
            "avatarUrls": {
